d).\n31\t- **GATE 1.** GREEN 1226.\n32\t- **REVIEW (2 independent, refute).** Both **GO, no regression.** Reviewer A traced both kill paths (hard-kill: keystone persist no-ops safely on the reaped worktree; reconcile-dead: keystone persist makes the plan set discoverable) + refuted the key grass risk (the keystone records the SAME research-lane effort as the v10 W5 code â€” byte-identical â€” so grass stays CONTAINED, not surfaced on the board). Reviewer B confirmed real unification (old duplicated code removed in 2/3 paths). Both independently re-verified non-vacuity (4â€“5/7 fail when persist is neutered). Corroborated CONCERN: `finish_to_build`â†’`auto_advance` double-invokes the keystone (double persist + ~5Ã— plan-set discovery).\n33\t- **FIX (investigated, REVERTED â€” the double-call is structural).** Attempted to make `auto_advance` the sole keystone invoker, but `finish_to_build` calls `capture_plan_set` ITSELF before delegating, and plan-set discovery reads the PERSISTED effort records â€” so `finish_to_build`'s keystone persist is what makes the just-authored plan set discoverable (removing it returns `auto_build:None` â€” proven by a failing test). Reverted + added a documenting comment so no future reader re-attempts it. The two keystone calls persist the SAME docs idempotently (one wasteful no-op re-persist; correct). + Hardened the W2 Playwright test's register-vs-paste-write race (poll until `pending_paste` is populated) â€” stress-verified **20/20** (was ~1/9 failing).\n34\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1226 passed, 1 skipped** (clean).\n35\t- **VERDICT: GO.** One asymmetry-class bug eliminated: all advance paths now share one persist+prompt keystone. Commit scoped (terminal_session.py, anchor_gui.py, effort_history.py, tests/test_handoff_unified_v11.py, tests/test_advance_research_to_plan_ui_v11.py).\n36\t\n37\t## Wave 4 â€” Verification hardening + healthcheck v11 + docs (PROJECT DONE) â€” âœ… GREEN\